s",16.4,"research",true,"3D Game","Pelican on a Bike","Claude Code · Three.js","/examples/pelican-bike-claude/","https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo/tree/main/pelican-bike","/GameMap/media/promo/chapter-3d.webp",8.2,8.8,"2D Game","Marvel Avengers: Infinity Strike","OpenGame · Phaser","/examples/opengame-marvel-platformer/","https://yelonhu.github.io/OpenGame-landing-page/","/GameMap/media/promo/chapter-2d.webp",0,1.1,{"_57":26,"_60":176,"_96":177,"_98":178,"_100":179,"_102":21,"_103":104,"_105":180,"_107":181,"_109":182,"_111":183,"_113":184,"_115":185,"_117":186},{"_57":28,"_60":85,"_96":149,"_98":150,"_102":19,"_103":151,"_105":152,"_107":153,"_109":154,"_111":155,"_113":156,"_115":157,"_117":158},{"_57":30,"_60":95,"_96":97,"_98":99,"_100":101,"_102":21,"_103":104,"_105":106,"_107":108,"_109":110,"_111":112,"_113":114,"_115":116,"_117":118},"TRON: EXONIX","description","A neon 3D territory-capture game built through Claude Code, Godot MCP, Blender MCP, and generated assets, with human design and playtest feedback.","engine","Godot 4.7 · GDScript","assetTools",[143,144,145,146,147,148],"track","category","ai-assisted","aiUse","The creator documents Claude writing gameplay, shaders, VFX, and UI while a human steers mechanics and materials. The repository includes the actual Godot game, generated assets, and the asset-generation scripts.","steps",[139,140,141,142],"tutorial",{"_58":137,"_124":138,"_134":109},"demo",{"_58":133,"_124":39,"_134":135,"_126":136},"source",{"_58":128,"_124":129,"_130":131,"_126":132},"evidence",{"_58":123,"_124":125,"_126":127},"resourceIds",[119,120,121,122],"claude-code","godot-engine","godot-mcp","mcp-for-blender","Read how the agent workflow was assembled","url","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix/blob/master/CLAUDE.md","note","The creator’s reproducible setup record explains the AI’s implementation work, human material review, generation tools, and local launch requirements.","Open the complete Godot game project","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix","scope","complete-project","Includes the Godot project, scripts, shaders, models, textures, audio, and generation scripts. Local play requires Godot 4.7 standard; API access is only needed to regenerate assets.","Play TRON: EXONIX","kind","playable","Creator-hosted Godot web build. Click to enter the grid, press Space to deploy, use the arrow keys to move, and Escape for the menu. A keyboard and a WebGL-capable browser are recommended.","Follow the creator’s complete workflow","https://www.top3d.ai/learn/claude-godot-mcp-3d-game","Play the web build and study territory capture, trail hazards, enemy movement, and sector progression.","Follow the creator’s tutorial from prototype through materials, audio, effects, and web export.","Read CLAUDE.md to understand the agent, Godot MCP, Blender review, and asset-generation workflow.","Open game/project.godot in Godot 4.7 and press F5; study the scripts alongside the included models, textures, and audio.","Blender","Nano Banana","PATINA","Tripo","Stable Audio","ElevenLabs","Study a generated action platformer with hero selection, combat skills, and a multi-stage brief.","Phaser 3 · TypeScript","ai-generated","This author-published OpenGame case connects a detailed action-game prompt to a live result and its generated source. Assess the implementation against the brief instead of treating the prompt as proof that every feature works.",[172,173,174,175],{"_58":170,"_124":163,"_134":171},{"_58":168,"_124":49,"_134":135,"_126":169},{"_58":165,"_124":166,"_126":167,"_130":131},{"_58":162,"_124":163,"_126":164},[159,160,161],"opengame","codex-browser-games","playwright-mcp","Author prompt and generation claim","https://github.com/leigest519/OpenGame#playable-demos","Listed in the authors’ single-prompt generated-game gallery, with the original platformer brief and an exact source download.","Download the exact platformer project","https://github.com/leigest519/OpenGame/raw/main/assets/downloads/demo_platformer_marvel.zip","Complete generated game archive, approximately 489.8 MB. Includes character selection and three level scenes; this is a large project download.","Play Infinity Strike","Direct author-hosted browser build. The gallery lists WASD / Space for movement, K for attack, and Q for the special skill.","Read the platformer generation prompt","prompt","Play the browser build and compare the selectable heroes and their combat feedback.","Read the original brief and turn its movement, skills, stages, and boss requirements into a short checklist.","Open the exact source archive and follow character selection into the three level scenes.","Choose one requirement to revise with an agent, then replay the relevant stage and check for regressions.","Moonlight & Mayhem","A 3D museum heist made with Codex: rescue two raccoon crewmates, evade security, stack the crew, and steal the Golden Sardine.","Three.js · JavaScript",[204],"Simon Willison documents giving Codex the game brief and image-generation access, then requesting a visual bug fix. The published project includes the game, generated textures, and the development transcript.",[200,201,202,203],{"_58":197,"_124":198,"_134":199},{"_58":195,"_124":53,"_134":135,"_126":196},{"_58":192,"_124":193,"_130":131,"_126":194},{"_58":189,"_124":190,"_126":191},[187,188,160],"codex","threejs","Read the published Codex transcript","https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/blob/main/transcript.md","The creator links this development record from the build account; it accompanies the game source rather than a generator-only repository.","Open the complete game project","https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/","Actual game source, committed textures, vendored Three.js, build notes, and transcript. No build step is required; use a local static HTTP server to run the repository.","Play Moonlight & Mayhem","Desktop: WASD or arrows to move, E to interact, Space or Shift to dash, Escape to pause. Mobile uses a touch stick and action buttons. Requires a WebGL-capable browser.","Read the creator’s build and fix log","https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/7/moonlight-mayhem/","build-log","Play the heist and trace crew rescue, security detection, interactions, and escape.","Read the creator’s build account and compare the original brief with the result.","Follow the transcript and commit history to study scene construction, generated art, and the visual bug fix.","Serve the complete repository locally, then study one mechanic and its supporting assets.","gpt-image-2",{"_206":207},"documents",{"_208":209,"_210":211},"en",[213,217,218,219,216,220,221,222,223,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,236,237,238,239,240,241,242,243,244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,215,252,214,253,254,255,256,257,258,259,260,261,262,263,264,265,266,267,268,269,270,271,272,273],"zh",[212,213,214,215,216],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-research","overview","catalog","contributing","media-sources","icon-sources","content-model","skills/level-design/SKILL","skills/level-design/LICENSE","design/design-system","design/v2/design-system","editorial-art-prompts","skills/level-design/refer